    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="1174" n="1148" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg1148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/6–1554: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-15T10:00:00+01:00">June 15, 1954—10 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dulte 181. Eyes only Secretary from Under Secretary. Reference Tedul 200.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d747-f1"/> I had also intended recommending Bonsal and Colonel
                    Dwan. Please do what you can to insure that military officer is Dwan<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d747-f2"/>.…</p>
                <pb facs="1175" n="1149" xml:id="pg1149"/>
                <p>Believe Korean phase will close out today generally as we planned. Recess would
                    only relate to Indochina phase, as assumed in Tedul 196.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d747-f3"/></p>
                <p>I would remain several days after Eden, if he follows his present plan, but would
                    attend no meetings. Have already discussed these matters with him and in general
                    way with Bidault before his departure. Do not know if Bidault intends to
                    return.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d747-f1" n="1" xml:id="d747-f1-content">
                <p>Summarized in <ref target="#pg1137">footnote 2, p. 1137</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d747-f2" n="2" xml:id="d747-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram Tedul 201, June 15, the Secretary informed Under Secretary Smith that
                    “Admiral Davis agrees that if small observer group is left at Geneva, Colonel
                    Dwan will remain with Bonsal.”</p>
                <p>In the same telegram the Secretary said he doubted “desirability of your
                    remaining since US has been the country which from the beginning has taken the
                    dimmest view of Geneva Conference and I would not like to see us the last to
                    leave. I hope you can get some rest before your return here where you will be
                    subjected to much Congressional questioning but I hope your rest could be
                    disassociated from Geneva Conference—perhaps based on your physically moving
                    elsewhere.” (396.1 GE/6–1554)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d747-f3" n="3" xml:id="d747-f3-content">
                <p>Dated June 14, <ref target="#pg1146">p. 1146</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
